cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  rieux_ampliseq: a multi-region CLI wrapper for nf-core/ampliseq
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Thiago
    family-names: Parente
    affiliation: Instituto Oswaldo Cruz, Fundação Oswaldo Cruz (Fiocruz)
repository-code: https://github.com/thiagoparentefiocruz/rieux_ampliseq
abstract: >-
  A staged bash wrapper that runs nf-core/ampliseq across every region of a
  multi-region 16S/ITS amplicon panel on an HPC cluster, measures the amplicon
  insert in the reads themselves to choose DADA2 truncation lengths, optionally
  runs the q2-sidle multi-region reconstruction, and consolidates the output
  into a single validated set of tables. Built for the QIAseq 16S/ITS Pro
  Screening Panel (96) — six 16S regions plus ITS1 — and driven by a primer
  table, so another panel supplies its own.
keywords:
  - metagenomics
  - amplicon sequencing
  - 16S rRNA
  - ITS
  - microbiome
  - DADA2
  - nextflow
  - multi-region
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-09-24'
